      "agent_input": "I'd like to review the Q3 2026 business report, please.",
      "agent_response": {
        "response": "Here is the **Meridian Analytics \u2014 Q3 2026 Business Report**:\n\n---\n\n## Overview\n- **Period:** July 1 \u2013 September 7, 2026\n- **Prepared by:** Rachel Kim (VP of Sales) & Claire Fontaine (CFO)\n- **Distribution:** Executive Team\n\n---\n\n## Executive Summary\n\nQ3 2026 marks another strong quarter for Meridian Analytics. Across the 15-person team, **14 deals were closed out of 22 opportunities**, generating **$1,040,000** in new contract value. The sales pipeline remains healthy with several high-value deals still in the pending stage. Customer support ticket volume held steady, with all critical issues resolved same-day.\n\n---\n\n## Sales Performance\n\n| Metric | Value |\n|---|---|\n| **Total Closed Revenue** | $1,040,000 |\n| **Top Region** | South \u2014 $468,000 in won deals |\n| **Win Rate** | 63.6% (above the 55% company target) |\n| **Active Opportunities** | 22 |\n| **Pending Deals** | 3 deals (~$240,000), expected to close by end of September |\n\nThe three-person field sales team \u2014 **James Okafor, Sofia Delgado, and Marcus Webb** \u2014 collectively worked all 22 active opportunities. Product mix shifted toward **Meridian Insights Pro** (majority of closed revenue), while **Meridian DataBridge** continues as a strong land-and-expand vehicle with upsell opportunities maturing in Q4.\n\n---\n\n## Key Highlights\n\n- \ud83c\udfc6 **Top Deal:** Sofia Delgado closed a **$198,000** Meridian Insights Pro contract with a Southern-region enterprise customer on September 5 (Deal D019).\n- \ud83d\udc65 **Team Headcount:** 15 employees across five departments \u2014 Sales (4), Engineering (5), Product (3), HR (1), Finance (2).\n- \u2705 **Support SLA:** All critical-priority tickets (TKT-004, TKT-011, TKT-015) were resolved within 24 hours.\n- \u26a0\ufe0f **License Utilization:** SKU-001 (Meridian Insights Pro) is at **94% capacity** \u2014 a procurement review is scheduled for October.\n\n---\n\n## Next Steps\n\n1. **Close pending deals** (D007, D013, D020, D022) before Q3 end.\n2. **Begin Q4 pipeline review** \u2014 target $1.2M in new ARR.\n3. **Resolve open support tickets** (TKT-013, TKT-016, TKT-019) ahead of quarterly customer success calls.\n4. **License capacity review** for SKU-001 and SKU-003 in early October.\n5. **HR to initiate two new engineering hire approvals** with Kenji Obi to support the Q4 roadmap.\n\n---\n\nThat's the full Q3 2026 report. Would you like me to dive deeper into any specific section, or pull up the underlying sales data or expense details for the quarter?",
